{"title":"Production Manager (Textile) Roadmap","role":"Production Manager (Textile)","summary":"A Production Manager (Textile) plans, supervises and improves textile manufacturing operations across processes such as spinning, weaving, knitting, dyeing, printing, processing and garment/textile finishing. The role combines textile engineering, production planning, quality management, machinery, process optimisation, supply-chain coordination, cost control and people leadership.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Textile Engineering / Technology"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment. B.Tech/B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology is a strong undergraduate route. However, Production Manager is normally a mid-career position, so graduates generally enter as production trainees, textile engineers, process engineers or supervisors before moving into managerial responsibility."}],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Current degree"},{"text":"B.Tech / B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology"}],[{"text":"Desired career"},{"text":"Production Manager (Textile)"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Engineering & Technology"}],[{"text":"Primary route"},{"text":"Textile Engineering → Production/Process → Supervisor → Production Manager"}],[{"text":"Core domains"},{"text":"Textile manufacturing, spinning, weaving/knitting, dyeing, finishing, quality, production planning"}],[{"text":"Major industries"},{"text":"Yarn, fabric, technical textiles, apparel, home textiles, dyeing & processing, synthetic fibres"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Textile fundamentals, mill exposure, production projects and quality/safety skills"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Production supervision, process optimisation, quality, lean manufacturing and plant operations"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Production Manager, Operations Manager, Manufacturing Excellence Specialist or Plant Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Lead smart, automated, sustainable and data-driven textile manufacturing"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are practical career-planning horizons rather than guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Mathematics, physics, chemistry, computing and engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"University + NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Technical calculations + Excel/Python"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Fibre science, textile materials and yarn fundamentals"},{"text":"Textile coursework + laboratory"},{"text":"Fibre/yarn testing reports"},{"text":"Textile foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Spinning, yarn manufacturing and textile machinery"},{"text":"Core courses + lab"},{"text":"Spinning-process project"},{"text":"Production understanding"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Weaving/knitting, fabric formation and machinery"},{"text":"Laboratory + industry visits"},{"text":"Fabric-production analysis"},{"text":"Manufacturing capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Dyeing, printing, finishing and chemical processing"},{"text":"Textile processing courses"},{"text":"Wet-processing project"},{"text":"Processing capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Textile testing, quality, production planning and industrial engineering"},{"text":"Industry internship + laboratory"},{"text":"QC + production-planning project"},{"text":"Operations readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Lean manufacturing, OEE, E